 Experiment 47: To Test a Mobile Banking REST API for Balance Enquiry Requests by Simulating Multiple Users and Verifying Status Codes, Response Data and Response Time

 AIM
To test a mobile banking REST API for balance enquiry requests by simulating multiple users and verifying status codes, response data, and response time using Apache JMeter.

ALGORITHM
1. Start Apache JMeter.
2. Create a new Test Plan.
3. Add a Thread Group to simulate multiple users.
4. Set the number of users, ramp-up period, and loop count.
5. Add an HTTP Request Sampler.
6. Select the GET method and enter the balance enquiry API URL.
7. Add the required authentication headers if needed.
8. Add Response Assertion to verify the HTTP status code.
9. Add JSON Assertion to validate the balance response data.
10. Add Summary Report to analyze response time and throughput.
11. Run the test and verify the results.

## CONFIGURATION

| Parameter | Value |
|---|---|
| Testing Tool | Apache JMeter |
| API Type | REST API |
| Request Method | GET |
| Number of Users | 10 |
| Ramp-up Period | 10 seconds |
| Loop Count | 5 |
| Request Type | Balance Enquiry |

**Sample API URL:**

```text
https://example.com/api/account/balance
```

*Note: Replace this sample URL with the actual authorized mobile banking API endpoint.*

## INPUT

Sample request:

```text
Method: GET
Endpoint: /api/account/balance
Account ID: 1001
